    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "The graph shows favourite subjects in two classes.\n(a) How many students in Class 6A chose Art?\n(b) Which class has more students choosing Maths, and how many more?\n(c) How many students chose Science altogether?\n(d) Which subject is most popular in Class 6B?\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]\n\\definecolor{seriesfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,10.8);\n\\draw[->] (0,0)--(7.5,0);\n\\foreach \\v in {0,2,4,6,8,10}{\\draw (-0.12,\\v)--(0,\\v);\\node[left,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (-0.15,\\v){$\\v$};}\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (0.7,0) rectangle (1.3,8);\n\\draw (1.4,0) rectangle (2,6);\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (3,0) rectangle (3.6,5);\n\\draw (3.7,0) rectangle (4.3,9);\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (5.3,0) rectangle (5.9,4);\n\\draw (6,0) rectangle (6.6,7);\n\\node[below] at (1.35,0){Maths};\n\\node[below] at (3.65,0){Art};\n\\node[below] at (5.95,0){Science};\n\\node[rotate=90] at (-0.95,5){Students};\n\\node at (3.65,-2.1){Subject};\n\\node at (3.65,14){Favourite subjects};\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (0.7,12) rectangle (1.1,12.8);\n\\node[right] at (1.2,12.4){Class 6A};\n\\draw (4.1,12) rectangle (4.5,12.8);\n\\node[right] at (4.6,12.4){Class 6B};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "(a) The legend identifies Class 6A as the light blue columns. The Art column ends halfway between $4$ and $6$, so $5$ students chose Art.\n\n(b) For Maths, Class 6A has $8$ students and Class 6B has $6$.\n$8-6=2$\nClass 6A has $2$ more students choosing Maths.\n\n(c) The Science columns show $4$ students in Class 6A and $7$ in Class 6B.\n$4+7=11$\nAltogether, $11$ students chose Science.\n\n(d) Class 6B's unfilled columns show Maths $6$, Art $9$ and Science $7$. Art is most popular in Class 6B."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "The graph compares points earned by two houses in four events.\n(a) Which event has the greatest difference between the houses?\n(b) Cedar's target is at least $28$ points. Did Cedar reach its target? By how many points?\n(c) Which house earned more points altogether, and by how many?\n(d) A student says, ‘Cedar earned more points than Maple in most events.’ Is the statement correct? Justify your answer.\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]\n\\definecolor{seriesfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,10.8);\n\\draw[->] (0,0)--(9.5,0);\n\\foreach \\v in {0,2,4,6,8,10}{\\draw (-0.12,\\v)--(0,\\v);\\node[left,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (-0.15,\\v){$\\v$};}\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (0.7,0) rectangle (1.3,7);\n\\draw (1.4,0) rectangle (2,4);\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (2.9,0) rectangle (3.5,4);\n\\draw (3.6,0) rectangle (4.2,10);\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (5.1,0) rectangle (5.7,8);\n\\draw (5.8,0) rectangle (6.4,8);\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (7.3,0) rectangle (7.9,6);\n\\draw (8,0) rectangle (8.6,9);\n\\foreach \\x/\\lab in {1.35/1,3.55/2,5.75/3,7.95/4}{\\node[below] at (\\x,0){$\\lab$};}\n\\node[rotate=90] at (-0.95,5){Points};\n\\node at (4.65,-2.1){Event};\n\\node at (4.65,14){House points};\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (1,12) rectangle (1.4,12.8);\n\\node[right] at (1.5,12.4){Cedar};\n\\draw (5.2,12) rectangle (5.6,12.8);\n\\node[right] at (5.7,12.4){Maple};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "The light blue columns represent Cedar; the unfilled columns represent Maple.\n\n(a) Subtract the smaller score from the larger score in each event.\n$\\begin{aligned}7-4&=3\\\\10-4&=6\\\\8-8&=0\\\\9-6&=3\\end{aligned}$\nEvent 2 has the greatest difference: $6$ points.\n\n(b) Add Cedar's four scores.\n$7+4+8+6=25$\n$28-25=3$\nCedar did not reach its target. It was $3$ points short.\n\n(c) Add Maple's four scores.\n$4+10+8+9=31$\n$31-25=6$\nMaple earned $6$ more points altogether.\n\n(d) Cedar is ahead only in Event 1. Maple is ahead in Events 2 and 4; Event 3 is tied. The statement is incorrect: Cedar is ahead in only $1$ of the $4$ events."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "The graph shows points earned by two teams in three activities. Team A's Games score is missing, so that column has not been drawn. Both teams earned the same total number of points. Find Team A's Games score.\n[tikz]\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]\n\\definecolor{seriesfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,10.8);\n\\draw[->] (0,0)--(7.5,0);\n\\foreach \\v in {0,2,4,6,8,10}{\\draw (-0.12,\\v)--(0,\\v);\\node[left,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (-0.15,\\v){$\\v$};}\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (0.7,0) rectangle (1.3,6);\n\\draw (1.4,0) rectangle (2,4);\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (3,0) rectangle (3.6,3);\n\\draw (3.7,0) rectangle (4.3,7);\n\\draw (6,0) rectangle (6.6,6);\n\\node[rotate=90] at (5.6,3){Missing};\n\\node[below] at (1.35,0){Quiz};\n\\node[below] at (3.65,0){Puzzle};\n\\node[below] at (5.95,0){Games};\n\\node[rotate=90] at (-0.95,5){Points};\n\\node at (3.65,-2.1){Activity};\n\\node at (3.65,14){Team points};\n\\draw[fill=seriesfill] (0.7,12) rectangle (1.1,12.8);\n\\node[right] at (1.2,12.4){Team A};\n\\draw (4.1,12) rectangle (4.5,12.8);\n\\node[right] at (4.6,12.4){Team B};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n[/tikz]",
        "solution_text": "Team B's unfilled columns show $4$, $7$ and $6$ points.\n$4+7+6=17$\nBoth teams therefore earned $17$ points.\n\nTeam A's known light blue columns show $6$ and $3$ points.\n$6+3=9$\nSubtract this known total from $17$.\n$17-9=8$\nTeam A's Games score is $8$ points."
      }
    ],
